__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
.roam/
internal/
.claude/
# Platform worktree scratch. Both names are listed on purpose: the platform is
# being renamed stoa -> prakteon, and the tooling that CREATES these directories
# (its swarm and bootstrap scripts) lives outside this repository. Dropping the
# old name here before that tooling is renamed would stop ignoring directories
# that are still being created, and they would surface in `git status` on a
# checkout the platform is driving. Remove `.stoa/` once the platform side no
# longer writes it.
.stoa/
.prakteon/
# Tool state that was never ignored here, so `git add .` after a tox run or a
# cache-writing linter staged the whole tree -- including any pip.conf inside
# it. scripts/secret_scan.py declines to open these directories and
# scripts/check.py's artifact_scan fails the build on tracking one; ignoring
# them removes the accident that made that pair matter.
.eggs/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
node_modules/

# Source-derived public documentation.
!/WIRING_COVERAGE.md
